cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  A companion paper is in preparation; this entry will be updated with
  the full citation once published.
title: >-
  Q-OPT: Quantum-Optimized Crypto-Agility for Attack-Resilient
  QKD-PQC-QRNG Networks
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "<Your Last Name>"
    given-names: "<Your First Name>"
    affiliation: "<Your Institution>"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-username>/qopt"
url: "https://github.com/<your-username>/qopt"
abstract: >-
  A security-constrained QUBO framework for adaptive routing and key
  management across hybrid quantum-key-distribution (QKD), post-quantum
  cryptography (PQC), and quantum-random-number-generation (QRNG)
  networks. Solved with QAOA (Qiskit), validated against classical
  baselines (exact, MILP, greedy, simulated annealing, tabular
  Q-learning), and confirmed on real IBM Quantum hardware
  (ibm_marrakesh).
keywords:
  - quantum key distribution
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - QAOA
  - QUBO
  - quantum optimization
  - network security
  - Qiskit
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-10"
